  "title": "How an Automotive Artist Pieced Together This Stunning McLaren M6GT",
  "summary": "“All real race cars have to be right-hand drive,” Randy Grubb says, beaming, as he opens the right-side door of the low-slung, V-8–powered missile he only recently completed. “They have to be, not because they’re built in England, not because they drive on the right side of the road, but because of the shifter linkage.” […]",
